    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "New Cumberland serves as the county seat of Hancock County, located along the Ohio River in the northern panhandle of West Virginia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Cumberland%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "New Cumberland fought a long political battle with New Manchester to become the permanent county seat, finally resolving the matter in 1884.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Cumberland%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Past local industry in New Cumberland included the manufacture of glassware, sewer pipe, and fire and paving bricks.",
